<tr><th>Call</th><th>Which method?</th><th>Why</th></tr>
<tr><td>m1()</td><td>var-arg</td><td>general method expects one int; you passed zero. Var-arg accepts any number including zero</td></tr>
<tr><td>m1(10, 20)</td><td>var-arg</td><td>general method does not match two ints</td></tr>
<tr><td>m1(10)</td><td>general method</td><td>both match, then general wins</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>Call that used to work</th><th>After replacement</th></tr>
<tr><td>m1()</td><td>invalid — method expects a 1-D array; you passed nothing</td></tr>
<tr><td>m1(10)</td><td>invalid — expects array, you passed an int</td></tr>
<tr><td>m1(10, 20, 30)</td><td>invalid</td></tr>
<tr><td>m1(new int[]{10, 20})</td><td>valid — you are passing an array</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>Direction</th><th>Valid replacement?</th></tr>
<tr><td>1-D array → var-arg</td><td>yes (old calls still work, new calls appear)</td></tr>
<tr><td>var-arg → 1-D array</td><td>no (zero-arg and loose-int calls break)</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>Declaration</th><th>We can call by passing</th><th>x becomes</th></tr>
<tr><td>m1(int... x)</td><td>a group of int values</td><td>1-D int array</td></tr>
<tr><td>m1(int[]... x)</td><td>a group of 1-D int arrays</td><td>2-D int array</td></tr>
<tr><td>m1(int[][]... x)</td><td>a group of 2-D int arrays</td><td>3-D int array</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>Iteration</th><th>x1</th><th>x1[0]</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>{10, 20, 30}</td><td>10</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>{40, 50, 60}</td><td>40</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>Declaration</th><th>Result</th><th>Why</th></tr>
<tr><td>m1(int... x)</td><td>valid</td><td>standard</td></tr>
<tr><td>m1(int ...x)</td><td>valid</td><td>space ignored</td></tr>
<tr><td>m1(int...x)</td><td>valid</td><td>no space needed</td></tr>
<tr><td>m1(int x...)</td><td>CE</td><td>... cannot follow the name (unlike int x[])</td></tr>
<tr><td>m1(int. ..x)</td><td>CE</td><td>three dots must stay together (“best friends”)</td></tr>
<tr><td>m1(int x, int... y)</td><td>valid</td><td>mix normal + var-arg</td></tr>
<tr><td>m1(String s, double... y)</td><td>valid</td><td>mix; var-arg last</td></tr>
<tr><td>m1(double... d, String s)</td><td>CE</td><td>var-arg must be last</td></tr>
<tr><td>m1(int... x, double... d)</td><td>CE</td><td>only one var-arg allowed</td></tr>
<tr><td>m1(int... x) and m1(int[] x) in one class</td><td>CE</td><td>cannot declare both m1(int[]) and m1(int...)</td></tr>
<tr><td>m1(int... x) and m1(int x) in one class</td><td>valid</td><td>different signatures; overload</td></tr>
</table>
</body></html>
